  margin: 0;
}

/* Our Card: Black borders and flat shadows */
.brutalist-card {
  background-color: #ffffff;
  border: 4px solid #000000;         /* 4px thick solid black line */
  padding: 24px;
  max-width: 400px;
  box-shadow: 8px 8px 0px 0px #000000; /* Flat offset black shadow (no blur) */
}

.card-title {
  margin-top: 0;
  font-size: 2rem;
  font-weight: 900;                  /* Super bold text */
  text-transform: uppercase;
}

.card-description {
  color: #333333;
  margin-bottom: 24px;
  line-height: 1.5;
}

/* Our Button: Bright contrast color and responsive click shadows */
.brutalist-button {
  background-color: #ffd60a;         /* Bright neon-brutalist yellow */
  border: 3px solid #000000;         /* 3px thick solid black border */
  font-size: 1rem;
  font-weight: 800;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  padding: 12px 24px;
  cursor: pointer;

  box-shadow: 4px 4px 0px 0px #000000; /* Flat shadow */

  /* Smooth animation transition when we hover/click */
  transition: transform 0.1s ease, box-shadow 0.1s ease;
}

/* HOVER: Move button slightly down and right, and shrink the shadow */
.brutalist-button:hover {
  transform: translate(2px, 2px);
  box-shadow: 2px 2px 0px 0px #000000;
}

/* ACTIVE (click): Move button fully down and right, remove shadow entirely */
.brutalist-button:active {
  transform: translate(4px, 4px);
  box-shadow: 0px 0px 0px 0px #000000;
}
</style>
```

### Let's dissect how this works:
1. **HTML Elements (`<div>`, `<h1>`, `<p>`, `<button>`)**: These are standard tags. Think of them as building blocks.
2. **HTML Classes (`class="brutalist-card"`)**: By giving elements a `class`, we can target them in our CSS.
3. **CSS Selectors (`.brutalist-card`)**: The dot `.` in CSS means "find the HTML element with this class name and apply these styles".
4. **Neo-Brutalist Shadow (`box-shadow: 8px 8px 0px 0px #000000`)**: Notice that the blur radius (the 3rd number) is set to `0px`. This keeps the shadow solid and sharp.
5. **Interactive pressed effect**: The `:hover` and `:active` CSS states offset the button (`translate(X, Y)`) while reducing the shadow by the same amount, making it look like a physical tactile button.

