```

Add that missing `}` right above the `:hover` block, save the file, and your server will instantly recover and compile correctly!

By default, buttons are what HTML calls **"Inline" elements**. This means they act exactly like words in a sentence—they sit side-by-side on the same line until they run out of room. 

To stack them vertically, we can use the same superpower we just learned: **Flexbox!**

Right now, your `.preview-container` is acting as a Flexbox room to center the card. We can *also* turn the card itself into a Flexbox container to organize the items inside it.

Go to `App.vue` and find your `.brutalist-card` CSS block. Add these three lines to it:

```css
.brutalist-card {
  background-color: #ffffff;
  border: 4px solid #000000;
  padding: 24px;
  width: 400px;
  box-shadow: 8px 8px 0px 0px #000000;

  /* Add these three lines! */
  display: flex;             /* Turn the card into a smart alignment zone */
  flex-direction: column;    /* Tell it to stack items Top-to-Bottom instead of Left-to-Right */
  gap: 16px;                 /* Automatically put 16 pixels of space between every item! */
}
```

### Why this is awesome:
By using `flex-direction: column`, we force everything inside the card to stack vertically. 
Even better, by using `gap: 16px;`, we don't need to write annoying margins on individual buttons anymore. The card just automatically inserts a perfect 16-pixel gap between any items you drop inside it!

