Your `App.vue` layout needs to become:
```
┌──────────────────────────────────┐
│           TOPBAR                 │  ← Full width across the top
├────────┬───────────────┬─────────┤
│SIDEBAR │  MAIN CONTENT │ RIGHT   │  ← Three columns below it
│        │               │ PANEL   │
└────────┴───────────────┴─────────┘
```

To achieve this, we wrap the three columns in their own box, and the topbar sits above that box. Also removing the toggle stuff and shrinking the sidebar.

Update your `App.vue` to this:

```vue
<style>
@import 'tailwindcss';
</style>

<script setup>
import topbar from './Components/layout/Topbar.vue'
import rightpanel from './Components/layout/rightpanel.vue'
import sidebar from './Components/layout/sidebar.vue'
</script>

<template>
  <div class="app-container">

    <!-- Row 1: Topbar spans the full width -->
    <topbar></topbar>

    <!-- Row 2: The three columns sit below -->
    <div class="app-body">
      <sidebar></sidebar>
      <main class="main-content">
        <router-view></router-view>
      </main>
      <rightpanel></rightpanel>
    </div>

  </div>
</template>

<style scoped>
.app-container {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column; /* Stack topbar ABOVE the body vertically! */
  height: 100vh;
  background-color: #faf6ee;
}

.app-body {
  display: flex; /* This makes the 3 columns sit side-by-side horizontally */
  flex-grow: 1; /* Take up all remaining vertical space below the topbar */
  overflow: hidden;
}

.main-content {
  flex-grow: 1;
  padding: 40px;
  overflow-y: auto;
}
</style>
